claims.statement_original:
Fix $\varepsilon>0$ and let $(\mu,\nu)\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{d_{x}})\times\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{d_{y}})$ be a pair of 4-sub-Weibull distributions with parameter $\sigma^{2}>0$. We have

\[
\begin{aligned}
\mathbb{E}\big[\big|\mathsf{S}_{\varepsilon}(\mu,\nu)-\mathsf{S}_{\varepsilon}(\hat{\mu}_{n},\nu)\big|\big] & \lesssim_{d_{x},d_{y}}\frac{1+\sigma^{4}}{\sqrt{n}}+\varepsilon\Bigg(1+\bigg(\frac{\sigma}{\sqrt{\varepsilon}}\bigg)^{9\left\lceil\frac{d_{x}}{2}\right\rceil+11}\Bigg)\frac{1}{\sqrt{n}} \\ \mathbb{E}\big[\big|\mathsf{S}_{\varepsilon}(\mu,\nu)-\mathsf{S}_{\varepsilon}(\hat{\mu}_{n},\hat{\nu}_{n})\big|\big] & \lesssim_{d_{x},d_{y}}\frac{1+\sigma^{4}}{\sqrt{n}}+\varepsilon\Bigg(1+\bigg(\frac{\sigma}{\sqrt{\varepsilon}}\bigg)^{9\left\lceil\frac{d_{x}\vee d_{y}}{2}\right\rceil+11}\Bigg)\frac{1}{\sqrt{n}}.
\end{aligned}
\]

Let $(\mu,\nu)\in\mathcal{P}(\mathcal{X})\times\mathcal{P}(\mathcal{Y})$, where $\mathcal{X}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d_{x}}$ and $\mathcal{Y}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d_{y}}$ are compact, and let $R=\mathrm{diam}(\mathcal{X})\vee\mathrm{diam}(\mathcal{Y})$. We have

\[
\begin{aligned}
\mathbb{E}\big[\big|\mathsf{D}(\mu,\nu)^{2}-\mathsf{D}(\hat{\mu}_{n},\nu)^{2}\big|\big] & \lesssim_{d_{x},d_{y}}\frac{R^{4}}{\sqrt{n}}+\big(1+R^{4}\big)n^{-\frac{2}{d_{x}\vee 4}}(\log n)^{\mathds{1}_{\{d_{x}=4\}}} \\ \mathbb{E}\big[\big|\mathsf{D}(\mu,\nu)^{2}-\mathsf{D}(\hat{\mu}_{n},\hat{\nu}_{n})^{2}\big|\big] & \lesssim_{d_{x},d_{y}}\frac{R^{4}}{\sqrt{n}}+\big(1+R^{4}\big)n^{-\frac{2}{(d_{x}\wedge d_{y})\vee 4}}(\log n)^{\mathds{1}_{\{d_{x}\wedge d_{y}=4\}}},
\end{aligned}
\]

and if $\mu,\nu$ are separated in the $(2,2)$-GW distance, i.e., $\mathsf{D}(\mu,\nu)>0$, then the same rates hold for estimating $\mathsf{D}$ itself, without the square.

Furthermore, the above rates are sharp in the sense that for any $n$ large enough, we have

\[
\begin{aligned}
\sup_{(\mu,\nu)\in\mathcal{P}(\mathcal{X})\times\mathcal{P}(\mathcal{Y})}\mathbb{E}\big[\big|\mathsf{D}(\mu,\nu)^{2}-\mathsf{D}(\hat{\mu}_{n},\nu)^{2}\big|\big] & \gtrsim_{\,d_{x},d_{y},R}\,n^{-\frac{2}{d_{x}\vee 4}} \\ \sup_{(\mu,\nu)\in\mathcal{P}(\mathcal{X})\times\mathcal{P}(\mathcal{Y})}\mathbb{E}\big[\big|\mathsf{D}(\mu,\nu)^{2}-\mathsf{D}(\hat{\mu}_{n},\hat{\nu}_{n})^{2}\big|\big] & \gtrsim_{\,d_{x},d_{y},R}\,n^{-\frac{2}{(d_{x}\wedge d_{y})\vee 4}}.
\end{aligned}
\]
